# Churn Intelligence Platform (Resume-Ready ML Project)

An end-to-end machine learning project that predicts customer churn and deploys predictions through a production-style API and dashboard.

## Why this stands out on a resume

- Framed as a real business problem (retention and revenue protection).
- Includes reproducible training, model selection, evaluation, and artifact versioning.
- Ships with a FastAPI inference service and a Streamlit analytics dashboard.
- Has automated tests for core ML behavior.

## Tech stack

- Python, scikit-learn, pandas, numpy
- FastAPI + Uvicorn (serving)
- Streamlit (analytics UI)
- Pytest (tests)

## Project structure

```
ML_Project/
  app/
    main.py
  dashboard/
    app.py
  src/churnintel/
    __init__.py
    data.py
    modeling.py
    train.py
    inference.py
  tests/
    test_modeling.py
  requirements.txt
  pyproject.toml
  README.md
```

## Quick start

1. Create and activate a virtual environment.
2. Install dependencies.
3. Train the model.
4. Run API and dashboard.

### Install

```powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -e .
```

### Train

```powershell
python -m churnintel.train --n-samples 8000
```

This creates artifacts in `artifacts/`:

- `model.joblib`
- `metrics.json`
- `leaderboard.csv`
- `feature_importance.csv`

### Run API

```powershell
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Open docs: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

### Run dashboard

```powershell
streamlit run dashboard/app.py
```

## Example prediction payload

```json
{
  "age": 38,
  "monthly_spend": 79.0,
  "tenure_months": 14,
  "support_tickets_90d": 4,
  "login_days_30d": 9,
  "contract_type": "month-to-month",
  "payment_method": "electronic-check",
  "region": "north"
}
```

## Resume bullets you can use

- Built an end-to-end churn prediction system (data generation, feature engineering, model selection, deployment) using Python, scikit-learn, and FastAPI.
- Implemented cross-validated model selection and evaluation pipeline, tracking ROC-AUC/F1 and feature importance for explainability.
- Deployed real-time inference API and interactive Streamlit dashboard, enabling business users to triage high-risk customers.
